=back

Returns string: the name of the selected haptic device. If no name can be found, this function returns NULL; call SDL_GetError() for more information.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

=head2 SDL_OpenHaptic

  my $result = SDL_OpenHaptic($instance_id);

C: C<< SDL_Haptic * SDL_OpenHaptic(SDL_HapticID instance_id) >>

Open a haptic device for use.

The index passed as an argument refers to the N'th haptic device on this system.

When opening a haptic device, its gain will be set to maximum and autocenter will be disabled. To modify these values use SDL_SetHapticGain() and SDL_SetHapticAutocenter().

=over

=item instance_id - unsigned integer. the haptic device instance ID.

=back

Returns SDL3::Haptic object or undef: the device identifier or NULL on failure; call SDL_GetError() for more information.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

