=head2 SDL_OpenHapticFromJoystick

  my $result = SDL_OpenHapticFromJoystick($joystick);

C: C<< SDL_Haptic * SDL_OpenHapticFromJoystick(SDL_Joystick * joystick) >>

Open a haptic device for use from a joystick device.

You must still close the haptic device separately. It will not be closed with the joystick.

When opened from a joystick you should first close the haptic device before closing the joystick device. If not, on some implementations the haptic device will also get unallocated and you'll be unable to use force feedback on that device.

=over

=item joystick - SDL3::Joystick object or undef. the SDL_Joystick to create a haptic device from.

=back

Returns SDL3::Haptic object or undef: a valid haptic device identifier on success or NULL on failure; call SDL_GetError() for more information.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

